Z||000006||1FST2M6||09-18-2000||08:53 AM||||Rods all about strange things!  ... humm lets see if i can take apart this puzzle and put it back together.. OK cool that worked.. now lets try and uuum another.. naa that too easy oh hell i'll just build an airplane...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  his car is beautiful! and SUPER CLEAN! i worked on it for a while only my back got dirty cause the floor was dusty! my hands stayed clean!   sweet ride Rod!    oh do you have a spruce aircraft accesories catalog? their in griffen, ga.?<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 09-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Shadow Wolf||09-20-2000||02:27 AM||||That just reminded me...<P>We just managed to drop the engine out of my buddy's '85 SC. (160,000+ miles).  Anyway, doing so, we noticed a lot of.. erm... things about the car.  (It should be noted he only paid $800 for it when it had only 60,000 miles on it)  <BR>ANYWAY, it turns out the previous owners had been driving the car over CEMENT BARRICADES and managed to hit one which dented the fuel tank, undercarriage, twisted a support arm in the engine cradle, and dropped the whole damn engine out of the car!  <P>Okay, that's part of it;<P>It also seems someone was playing with a cutting torch.  Not only did they remove the mounts for hte trailer hitch, what we though was a big ugly crack in the frame, had cutting torch residue on the bloody thing!  This poor car had been punished since the day it was driven off the dealer's lot!  At least it ran well for my buddy for 6 years before the engine died.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
